Z||000000||mblackwell||01-18-2001||03:10 PM||||I was just wondering if anyone else uses the space on either side of the guage housing as a cupholder.  They are the perfect size for Wendy's Biggie drinks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever2||01-18-2001||03:24 PM||||Yes, tgowens does that.  I think it's too precarious.<BR>Read on:<BR>- <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004601.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004601.html</A> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||stimpy||01-18-2001||11:53 PM||||Hell yeah, do it all the time.  But one time I put a Del Rancho cup in and was not careful about pushing it down far enough.  Took off a little to aggresively and got a Dr. Pepper bath. <P>Other good fits are the Taco Bell & 7eleven plastic 32 oz cups that taper at the bottom. Solid.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||01-18-2001||11:59 PM||||Most 20oz paper coffee cups also fit perfectly.  Just make sure you have a lid  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||01-19-2001||12:51 AM||||I do it, but only with the big taco bell cups.  I'm too afraid of a paper cup squeezing through and splashing everything...||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||01-19-2001||12:56 AM||||yep, Chuck is right - I use it all the time - I use the aluminum travel mugs though - tapered is a must!! - and, a mug will fit on either side of the gauge pod (on BOTH sides if you are <I>really</I> thirsty!! of course, I usually drink coffee on my trips so the thermal mug is a must for me -- the cold drinks go in the cooler on the console!||||reg||1
